public void log(int[] numbers, int[] names) {   //the runtime complexity is O(n)

    for (int j = 0; j<names.length; j++){
       System.out.println(names[j]);
    }
    for (int i = 0; i < numbers.length; i++) {
       System.out.println(numbers[i]);
    }

}

Note: it still linear
      O(n+m) = O(n)

